# Data conversion between mebibyte and megabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between mebibyte and megabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MiB to 1.0485MB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 1.5728MB; backward, converting 1MB to 0.9536MiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 1.4305MiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(forward_whole->to(MB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(forward_fractional->to(MB))
backward_whole: int = 1MB
print(backward_whole->to(MiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(backward_fractional->to(MiB))

<<< stdout
1.0485MB
1.5728MB
0.9536MiB
1.4305MiB

<<< stderr
